  "body": "From the second read of PR #3468 after its merge (comment 7081679987 on that PR). The read found no defect in the posted blocks. Four points depend on the control (the maintainer's Fanuc 31i-A5) and the cited public manual does not answer them.\n\n1. The post writes `S M3` at the start of the section and then `M29 S` while the spindle turns. Does the control accept `M29` with the spindle on, or is `M5` necessary before it?\n2. After `G80` ends the rigid mode, some controls leave the spindle stopped. The post treats the spindle as on, and writes `S M3` again only when the stream gives a new speed. Is a restart necessary before the next operation of the same section?\n3. If the speed changes inside a tapping section, `M29 S` has the new speed but `S M3` is not written again.\n4. The feed must be the pitch times the speed. The post does not check `F / S` against the pitch of the tap; the value comes from the stream. A check with a refusal is possible.\n\nThe option \"Rigid tap M29 before G84\" is off by default.\n\nNecessary work: the result of a test on the control for points 1 and 2 (an air cut is sufficient), then the change of `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` that the result needs, and the check of point 4.\n\nRefs #2603\n",
